 "body_a_old": "Therapeutic massage combines focused work with time to relax. I start with what brought you in. You can ask me to stay with one area, such as your neck and shoulders, or to work more broadly, and the plan can change as you give me feedback.<br><br>Research suggests that massage therapy may help reduce pain in some conditions and may improve certain movement-related outcomes in studied pain populations.<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39008297/\">[1]</a><a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27165971/\">[2]</a> Studies of sports massage have found small improvements in flexibility and exercise-related muscle soreness.<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32426160/\">[3]</a> Brief massage has been studied for short-term relaxation.<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32901072/\">[4]</a> Regular massage was associated with improved well-being in a small four-week study of older adults.<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17709060/\">[5]</a><br><br>Research has explored massage in several adult groups, including family caregivers.<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27165971/\">[2]</a><a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33919371/\">[6]</a><a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39558520/\">[7]</a><a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31003683/\">[8]</a> Research has also examined massage in relation to stress and quality-of-life measures in specific adult groups.<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27901219/\">[9]</a><a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33053005/\">[10]</a><a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17709060/\">[5]</a></p>",
 "body_a_new": "Therapeutic massage combines focused work with time to relax. I start with what brought you in. You can ask me to stay with one area, such as your neck and shoulders, or to work more broadly, and the plan can change as you give me feedback.<br><br>Research suggests that massage therapy may help reduce pain in some conditions and may improve certain movement-related outcomes in studied pain populations.<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39008297/\">[1]</a><a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27165971/\">[2]</a> Studies of sports massage have found small improvements in flexibility and exercise-related muscle soreness.<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32426160/\">[3]</a> Brief massage has been studied for short-term relaxation.<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32901072/\">[4]</a> Regular massage was associated with improved well-being in a small four-week study of older adults.<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17709060/\">[5]</a><br><br>Some studies have looked at massage in family caregivers.<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31003683/\">[6]</a> Research has also examined massage in relation to stress and quality-of-life measures in specific adult groups.<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/27901219/\">[7]</a><a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33053005/\">[8]</a><a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/17709060/\">[5]</a></p>",
 "body_b_old": "People often book therapeutic massage for everyday muscle tension and stiffness, or simply to make time to slow down. Some also seek focused work for neck or shoulder discomfort. Research suggests massage may be helpful for some people with neck or shoulder pain, though the benefits may last only a short time.<a href=\"https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/massage-therapy-what-you-need-to-know\">[11]</a> Massage has also been studied for low-back pain, although the evidence is limited.<a href=\"https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/massage-therapy-what-you-need-to-know\">[11]</a> Before I begin, I ask about your preferences and anything I should know about your health. You can request lighter pressure, a different focus, or a pause at any time.</p>",
 "body_b_new": "People often book therapeutic massage for everyday muscle tension and stiffness, or simply to make time to slow down. Some also seek focused work for neck or shoulder discomfort, and I adapt the pace and pressure to what suits you. Research on massage for neck and shoulder pain is mixed. It may help some people for a short time,<a href=\"https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/massage-therapy-what-you-need-to-know\">[9]</a> but a 2024 Cochrane review found that, for neck pain, massage probably makes little or no difference compared with a placebo massage.<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38415786/\">[10]</a> A subgroup analysis in that review favored higher doses (eight or more sessions of at least 30 minutes over four weeks), which suggests that regular sessions may matter.<a href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/38415786/\">[10]</a> Massage has also been studied for low-back pain, although the evidence is limited.<a href=\"https://www.nccih.nih.gov/health/massage-therapy-what-you-need-to-know\">[9]</a> Before I begin, I ask about your preferences and anything I should know about your health. You can request lighter pressure, a different focus, or a pause at any time.</p>",
 "faq_old": "<!-- wp:uagb/faq-child {\"block_id\":\"d6b5c6d7\",\"question\":\"Can I Ask You to Focus on My Neck and Shoulders?\",\"answer\":\"Yes. Tell me at the start where you would like the focus, and you can change it at any point during the session. For anything new, severe, or worrying, please see a doctor first.\",\"icon\":\"chevron-up\",\"iconActive\":\"chevron-down\"} /--></div>\n<!-- /wp:uagb/faq -->",
 "faq_new": "<!-- wp:uagb/faq-child {\"block_id\":\"d6b5c6d7\",\"question\":\"Can I Ask You to Focus on My Neck and Shoulders?\",\"answer\":\"Yes. Tell me at the start where you would like the focus, and you can change it at any point during the session. For anything new, severe, or worrying, please see a doctor first.\",\"icon\":\"chevron-up\",\"iconActive\":\"chevron-down\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:uagb/faq-child {\"block_id\":\"3d8a5f21\",\"question\":\"How Is Therapeutic Massage Different From Deep Tissue Massage?\",\"answer\":\"Therapeutic massage gives steady attention to the places where you feel tension, at a pace and pressure that suit you. Deep tissue massage uses focused strokes and sustained pressure on areas that stay tight. I check in about pressure in both, and each is described on its own page.\",\"icon\":\"chevron-up\",\"iconActive\":\"chevron-down\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:uagb/faq-child {\"block_id\":\"a94c7e03\",\"question\":\"Can I Change the Pressure During a Session?\",\"answer\":\"Yes. You can ask for lighter pressure, a different focus, or a pause at any time, and I will adjust.\",\"icon\":\"chevron-up\",\"iconActive\":\"chevron-down\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:uagb/faq-child {\"block_id\":\"5b1f6d98\",\"question\":\"Where Do Sessions Take Place?\",\"answer\":\"Sessions take place in Mt. Tabor, Portland. I do not currently travel to clients.\",\"icon\":\"chevron-up\",\"iconActive\":\"chevron-down\"} /-->\n\n<!-- wp:uagb/faq-child {\"block_id\":\"e07a3c52\",\"question\":\"How Do I Book a Session?\",\"answer\":\"Use the Contact page to reach me by phone or email, and tell me what you would like. I will reply to arrange a time.\",\"icon\":\"chevron-up\",\"iconActive\":\"chevron-down\"} /--></div>\n<!-- /wp:uagb/faq -->",
