 "faq_text": "How Is Therapeutic Massage Different From Deep Tissue Massage? Therapeutic massage gives steady attention to the places where you feel tension, at a pace and pressure that suit you. Deep tissue massage uses focused strokes and sustained pressure on areas that stay tight. I check in about pressure in both, and each is described on its own page. Can I Change the Pressure During a Session? Yes. You can ask for lighter pressure, a different focus, or a pause at any time, and I will adjust. Where Do Sessions Take Place? Sessions take place in Mt. Tabor, Portland. I do not currently travel to clients. How Do I Book a Session? Use the Contact page to reach me by phone or email, and tell me what you would like. I will reply to arrange a time.",
